      "side": 1,
      "message": "Fixed.\n\nI spent some time looking at the code around this and could not see how it could be anything other than 32/64 bit. This method returns CompileMultiTargets, that property is only set in archMutator to a Target slice returned by decodeMultilibTargets(..) which can only return lib32/lib64 and (if compile_multilib was set to \"common\") then the common architecture for the target os\u0027s. As the sdk module type hard codes compile_multilib to \"both\" I ignored the \"common\" possibility. So, you\u0027re right that the documentation is inaccurate.\n\nI personally find the MultiTargets name confusing as it seems like it should be related to multilib. Then again, I find multilib itself confusing as it is a pretty generic name that refers to 32/64 bit. Is there a better name to use to describe the 32/64 bit variants/targets?\n\nWould it make sense to rename MultiTargets() and CompileMultiTargets to say ...MultiArchTargets() or ExtraArchTargets()?",
      "parentUuid": "58ccfebd_a96b13c9",
